  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, the Mark 93 pattern. A blank options position means the standard bellows by the sheet's own note, so the empty code is carried; a build with no options assembles with a trailing dash, held for John as on the other 93 sheets. The sheet's combine rule says alphabetical order yet its own example prints 93TH-075-N-PL, P before L, so the pair is carried as the example prints it and the conflict is held for John. The BSPT and EN ISO 228-1 threaded ends are available upon request by their own footnote.",
